\par section\cell }\pard \qj\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar\intbl {\fs16 \cell }\pard \widctlpar\intbl {\fs16 \row }\pard \qj\sl-240\slmult0\widctlpar {\fs16 
\par }\pard \qj\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar \sect \sectd \psz9\linex0\headery706\footery706\colsx709\endnhere \pard\plain \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 
We can see that the whole restructuring within the enterprise was a natural process from one side. The changes in the organisational structure followed the changes in the legal form. The same processes we can observe in many other enterprises. 
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
The enlargement of the main industrial workshops and the unification of them into one production unit have led to the elimination of the duplication of the functions of some of the workshops, and also reduced the number of disputes. (For example, the old 
dispute between the providing spare parts in the Kukino and Popugai areas. There is no division for competitive workshops now, they became a part of one production and the Director of Production is now interested in the uniform provision of both sites).

\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
Besides, new departments were constructed. So, the changes in the enterprise structure were characterised by the new market relations. Some of the departments were constructed on the basis of western models (for example, a Venture Department). Thus, the m
ain tendency was the correspondence with the present situation. That is why the role of the traditional departments
, who played a decisive role in the past command-administrative relations was diminished with the new market relations. And the role of the new departments as for example, Department of Marketing or Department of External Co-operation increased.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
From the other side, the whole process of restructuring was a part of further centralisation of power in the hands of the top managers and especially of the General Director. All process of reorganisation were organised in a such way that all new structur
es supported the unlimited power of the general director. He tried to destroy any threats to his position as soon as possible.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar Besides, the new western approaches together with market mechanisms were combined in the new structure with the old traditional approach to organise the {\i place for a certain person}
, and the whole process of restructuring was organised with the help of informal relations, which played a decisive role in the whole process. 
\par \pard\plain \s2\sb360\sa120\sl480\slmult1\keepn\widctlpar \b\i\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc404268001}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc407554732}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc408378697}Privatisation and transition of the plant into a share-holding company. September 1994
{\*\bkmkend _Toc404268001}{\*\bkmkend _Toc407554732}{\*\bkmkend _Toc408378697}
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 
In 1994 there was a further step in the privatisation of the plant, with its conversion from leasehold to a joint-stock company. The program of the transition of the plant into a private company was organised under the direct leadership of the General Dir
ector. The documents had been prepared in 1992 and sent to the government authorities. But the documents lay in the government offices for almost two years, before the plant was allowed to be privatised. The plant was privatised in September 1
994. If we consider the whole preparation for privatisation within the plant, we can see that there were some tendencies towards transforming the enterprise into a competitive market enterprise: production was reorganised, some new departments were formed
 (for example, the department of marketing). Thus, the upper management, and mainly the General Director, was one of the main leading forces of the future changes.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar In order to analyse the main causes of the conversion of the plant Remet into a share-holding company, it is necessary to stress several positive features of its new legal form:
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 1. If the share-holder decided to leave this company, he can sell his shares to the company.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 2. The new organisational form gives the possibility to attract quite big financial resources from investors without being dependent on the financial support of the banks.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar Now, consider the process of development of the plant since 1994. The registered capital of the company on the 25.05.95 was 476 347 000 roubles, which consisted o
f 422 641 normal shares and 53 706 privileged shares (I share = 1 thousand roubles).
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
The first issue of shares was registered in the Department of Finance of Moscow on the 4th of September, 1995, a total amount of 320 mln. roubles. The second issue was registered on the 2nd of February 1996, total amount 880 mln. roubles, among them ordin
ary shares (total amount 580 mln. roubles) and privileged shares (total amount 300 mln. roubles).
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar Thus, the plant was organised into a share-holding company. The main gover
ning body of the shareholding company became the annual Conference of Shareholders that can elect the Directors, change the regulations, approve reorganisation and so on. Once a year the company should organise the Conference of Shareholders. The main gov
erning organ of the company between Conferences was the Council of Directors.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar The first conference of share-holders of the Remet company was 20.05.1995. 526 share-holders took part in this meeting. The share-holders approved a report on the activity of the 
governing body and the annual balance of the enterprise and made a decision to set the rate of dividend payment as 2 238 roubles per 1 share for 1994, which was an annual rate of 446 % per year. (Note: the deposit rate of the financial banks in the same y
ear was 120-150% per year).
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar In 1995 the plant developed at very high speed. The sum of registered capital increased in 3.8 times and by 1.01.1996 reached 38.9 billion roubles. Balance profit was:
\par \pard \qr\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar Table 5.1
\par \pard\plain \s34\qc\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 Balance profit of the plant Remet in 1995-1996. 
\par (mln. roubles.)
