\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrh\brdrs\brdrw15 \trbrdrv\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cellx1749\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 
\cellx3498\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cellx5247\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cellx6996\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl
\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 \cellx8550 \pard\plain \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 18 573{\f133 \cell }3 499 {\f133 \cell }9 764{\f133 \cell }23 525{\f133 \cell }\pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl 30 304\cell \pard\plain 
\widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 \row \pard\plain \s34\qj\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 
The process of share distribution was conducted without any difficulties, there were not any disputes about this question. According to experts, around 10% of the shares belonged to the General director, another 10 % of the shares were in the holders had 
no more than 60 % of the shares. 
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar By the time of the second Conference of Share-holders, which was organised on 25.05.1996 on the plant, there were 1551 registered share-holders, who possessed 414 327 shares, among them 347 261 ordinary shares.

\par Very soon people felt the positive sides of the possession of shares. The dividends per share were paid each quarter of the year. And the pensioners first considered that it is profitable to get shares. So now, they began to buy shares as one of the ways 
to increase their incomes.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar If before the plant always had to consult with Metro authorities about everything, now it received much more freedom, for example in formation its own payment system, clients\rquote 
 connections and soon. At the same time, although all employees automatically became shareholders, there were not any substantial changes in their rights. In fact not one of the workers could explain the difference between th
e modern situation and the past. A General meeting of the Leaseholders was organised once a year. The Collective Agreement of the leaseholding enterprise had to be revised once every 3 years.
\par \pard\plain \s2\sb360\sa120\sl480\slmult1\keepn\widctlpar \b\i\f5\fs28\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc404268002}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc407554733}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc408378698}The economic situation in the plant since 1994{\*\bkmkend _Toc404268002}
{\*\bkmkend _Toc407554733}{\*\bkmkend _Toc408378698} 
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 The plant had quite big problems approximately till the end of 1993. The difficulties of the past influenced the plant\rquote 
s production. Only at the beginning of 1994 did the situation within the plant become stabilised and the plant began to show an almost unique example in 
Russia: in the situation of total production failure all over the country, there was a stable increase in production. 
\par \pard \sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar The general dynamic of production you can see in Diagram 5.1.{\fs28  }
\par \pard \sa120\widctlpar\pvpara\posy0\dxfrtext180\dfrmtxtx180\dfrmtxty0 Diagram 5.1. {\b Dynamic of the repair of the carriages 1994-1996
