\s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl\pvpara\posy0\dxfrtext180\dfrmtxtx180\dfrmtxty0 {\fs22 82,2\cell 16,4\cell }\pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl\pvpara\posy0\dxfrtext180\dfrmtxtx180\dfrmtxty0 {\fs22 26,6\cell }\pard 
\s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl\pvpara\posy0\dxfrtext180\dfrmtxtx180\dfrmtxty0 {\fs22 43,0\cell }\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 \row \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar\pvpara\posy0\dxfrtext180\dfrmtxtx180\dfrmtxty0 
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
As we can see in 1993 mainly, workshops fulfilled the plan in the last ten days, and this is true for almost all the workshops. The carriages workshops repaired the majority of their production output in the third ten days (more then 80%).
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar The present situation in the plant from this point of view became much more organised, and the departments usually fulfilled the repairs according to the planned program without firefighting at the end of the month.

\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar Besides, the time for the repair of the carriages was also reduced, mainly because of a more effective way of utilising the repair places.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
One of the key factors of stabilising the rhythm of production in 1996 was the very stable work of the production of spare parts within the plant. In order to improve the planning and control of providing materials, the production-operating department was
 re-structured, and within this department a bureau for preparing production was constructed.
\par From the very beginning 
of the disruptions of the economic connections in the former USSR, the plant was re-oriented into the organisation of a self-providing system of spare parts. That is why the mechanical-assembly workshop became responsible for providing spare parts for the
 needs of the plant.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar In 1996 there was a further tendency within the plant to reduce the number of parts produced by external partners. The number of the parts produced by the mechanical-assembly shop increased by 201 units. 
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar In 1996 there were still 79 parts made by external partners, among them:
\par 6 - because of the lack of equipment,
\par 22- because of the lack of rigging,
\par 51- because of internal reasons within the mechanical-assembly workshop.
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar In 1997 the plant will maintain the tendency to reduce the number of parts delivered by external enterprises, and it was planned that by the beginning of 1998 the plant would provide the whole range of spare parts.

\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar Another factor proving the tendency towards stabilisation in the plant was the reduction of labour turnover.
\par \pard\plain \s3\qj\sb240\sa120\sl480\slmult1\keepn\widctlpar \b\f5\lang2057 {\*\bkmkstart _Toc404268003}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc407554734}{\*\bkmkstart _Toc408378699}Stabilisation of labour turnover{\*\bkmkend _Toc404268003}{\*\bkmkend _Toc407554734}
{\*\bkmkend _Toc408378699}
\par \pard\plain \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 In 1995 the staff structure of the plant was constructed in the following way: 
\par \pard\plain \s34\qj\widctlpar \f40\lang2057 
\par \trowd \trgaph108\trleft-108 \cellx7200\cellx8748 \pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl managers (heads of the departments, workshops and so on) \cell \pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl 12,1%\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 \row \trowd 
\trgaph108\trleft-108 \cellx7200\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 specialists \cell \pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl 13,3%\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 \row \pard\plain \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 
clerks\cell \pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl 0,4%\cell \pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 \row \trowd \trgaph108\trleft-108 \cellx7200\cellx8748 \pard\plain \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 workers \cell \pard \s34\qj\widctlpar\intbl 74,2%\cell 
\pard\plain \widctlpar\intbl \f40\lang2057 \row \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar 
\par \pard \qj\sa120\sl480\slmult1\widctlpar In 1996 the plant hired 336 employees, including 272 workers and 64 specialists and 240 people left, of whom 203 were workers and 37 specialists. 
